 "context": [
  {
   "h": "Love's arrows",
   "body": "<p>In Greek and Roman myth Cupid's arrows made whoever they struck fall helplessly in love: Apollo's love for Daphne, for example, began with one of them. When Psyche pricks her own thumb on one of her husband's arrows, she falls in love in the most literal way possible, with Love himself.</p><p>Curiosity (<em>curiositas</em>) is one of the great themes of the whole novel. Its hero, Lucius, is turned into a donkey because he is too curious about magic, and Psyche's curiosity is about to cost her dearly too.</p>"
